TI  - CHARACTERISTICS OF HABITATS OF MICROTUS-BRANDT-II IN THE EAST KHANGAI
T2  - ZOOLOGICHESKY ZHURNAL
AB  - Habitats where Brandt''s voles survived during years with depressed populations covered up to 10 ha in area, in regions of small sod steppe grazed by cattle in the upper links of the erosion net (slope-banked valleys of the spring and river sources) in the East Khangai (Mongolia). Habitat dynamics was followed over 3 yr. Population structure, 1 habitat utilization and migrations were determined by marking techniques. Similar survival habitats were found in the other Khangai regions. The restoration of numbers probably takes place at the expense of the reproducing and migrating population in survival habitats only, which supports measures for the control of this pasture pest.
