TI  - The investigation of digesta passage through gastrointestinal tract using oral multiple-dose introduction of plastic markers to voles
T2  - ZOOLOGICHESKY ZHURNAL
AB  - The digesta passage through the gastrointestinal tract was studied using the oral multiple-dose introduction of small fragments of variegated plastic to the voles, Lasiopodomys mandarinus, Microtus rossiaemeridionalis. M. arvalis arvalis, and M. arvalis obscurus. The duration of the experiments was 6-8 hours. The amount of the markers in each segment of the digestive tract was counted after killing and dissection of the animals. The sequence of the marked food evacuation was found can be disrupted. The last introduced marker might pass faster than the previous ones. The nonuniform evacuation of alternate consumed foodstuffs may take place due to the fact that one part of digesta is localized in forestomach and caecum, where it is exposed to microbial fermentation. while the other part passes by these chambers through the grandular stomach and small intestine. The localization of the consumed foodstuffs in different digestive organs (segments of the digestive tract) and separation of digesta into rapidly and slowly passing portions provide the extraction of nutrients from poor plant food in maximal full measure.
