AU  - JONES, RM
AU  - MOTT, JJ
TI  - POPULATION-DYNAMICS IN GRAZED PASTURES
T2  - TROPICAL GRASSLANDS
AB  - The role of population dynamics in determining the species composition and botanical stability of grazed pastures is discussed. Examples, mainly from tropical pasture species, are given to show how different stages of the life cycle of pasture plants, such as recruitment and death, have been altered by management and environment. Studies of population dynamics in pastures could aid in the extrapolation of results from grazing studies, in predicting improved management strategies and in highlighting objectives for plant introduction and breeding. Suggestions are made as to when population studies are appropriate in pasture research and about the way experimental studies could be planned.
