TI  - Alluvial meadows under changing management: Their degradation and restoration
T2  - WETLANDS: MONITORING, MODELLING AND MANAGEMENT
CP  - International Conference Wetlands - Monitoring, Modelling and Management
AB  - Alluvial meadows in Europe have been largely destroyed or degraded due conversion into arable land, by drainage, eutrophication, abandonment or overexploitation. For their restoration, the following methods can be considered, often in combination: re-establishment of traditional management (mowing, grazing); rewetting (re-establishment of flooding and/or ground seepage regime); top soil removal (sod cutting) to decrease nutrient content; direct sowing of target species; and application of mown plant material or topsoil, or transport of monoliths from nearby species-rich reference sites. Relevant literature is reviewed and both degradation and restoration are illustrated by results of several case studies.
