AB  - A study on efficient visualization and real-time interactivity of large-scale scenes was discussed in this paper. Introducing the parallel processing technology, we present a paralletizable strategy with the pipeline algorithm, realize this parallel algorithm based on shared-memory, and then apply this program to Test Site, Peking Olympic Games planning mixed scenes, including real-time rendering, dynamically textures loading, quickly browsing and so on. The results show a running performance and real-time interactivity improvement of DEPS when using this algorithm.
   The parallel program of this paper was developed and running on a Silicon Graphics multiprocessor, Onyx 3200, with four MIPS R12000 processors and InfiniteReality3 graphic accelerator, under IRIX 6.5 operating system.
